The following components in this repository are derived from or inspired by
gpt-pp-team's design and source code:

  * `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
    - Inspired by gpt-pp-team `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
    - Borrowed: 4-job CI pattern (lint / syntax / secret-scan), ruff
      `--select=E9,F63,F7,F82` flag set, secret-scan via grep with concatenated
      patterns to avoid self-matching, absolute-path sweep step.
    - Adapted: token patterns rewritten for team-register's env vars
      (EFUNCARD_TOKEN / NODECARD_TOKEN / X988_TOKEN / SMS_API_KEY /
      MAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN / LLM_API_KEY / SESSION_SECRET); path patterns
      changed to /Users/* (macOS dev box) instead of /home/kali.

  * `src/services/decline_retry_service.py` (planned, not yet committed)
    - Inspired by gpt-pp-team `CTF-pay/retry_house_decline.py`
    - Borrowed: per-attempt time-on-page jitter strategy (`base_min * attempt`),
      terminal-decline vs challenge vs session-inactive result classification.
    - Adapted: function-level retry instead of subprocess respawn; integrates
      with team-register's existing `_classify_decline()` and `Run` model.

  * `docs/research/risk-control-insights.md` (planned, not yet committed)
    - Inspired by gpt-pp-team `docs/anti-fraud-research.md`
    - Borrowed: methodology and section structure (probe vs ban layer model,
      multi-dimensional scattering: IP / domain / payment / timing).
    - NOT borrowed: any specific empirical data, IP/account anonymized samples,
      or production statistics. team-register documents its own design only.

